@table @code
@item initrd-binary
binary size (measured in CI on every build). The binary the initrd carries: `bin/fairing` of the flake's `fairing-initrd` package, built by nixpkgs without default features as the NixOS module builds it (decided at G1, 2026-10-16); CI's `nix` job. A cargo build of the same features comes out smaller and is reported by the size job only.
@item theme-artefact
artefact size (measured in CI on every build). The reference theme compiled with `fairing theme compile themes/steelbore.ncl`; CI's size job.
@item first-frame
cold-start latency (measured on the reference machine). `first_frame_ms` of `fairing preview --backend drm --seconds 5 --json` on a free VT: process start to the first frame on screen. `cargo xtask measure --preview-drm` reads it (RELEASING.md).
@item artefact-load
theme load time (measured on the reference machine). `load_ms` of `fairing theme compile themes/steelbore.ncl --json`, the median time to decode the reference artefact from its bytes. `cargo xtask measure --theme-compile` reads it.
@item sigterm-release
release latency (measured on the reference machine). `release_ms` of the stage-2 splash report that ended in `handoff`, from the journal of a reference boot: the tick that saw greetd's SIGTERM to the output released. `cargo xtask measure` reads it.
@item fbdev-fallback
fallback latency (measured on the reference machine). `first_frame_ms` of `fairing preview --backend auto --json` with the DRM devices withheld (`/dev/dri` hidden by a mount namespace), so the failed DRM attempt and the fbdev first frame both fall inside it: an upper bound. `cargo xtask measure --preview-fbdev` reads it.
@item reacquire
re-acquire latency (measured on the reference machine). `reacquire_ms` of the splash reports of a reference boot: the longest a lost output (the simpledrm-to-i915 swap) took to present again, from the first frame that found it lost; `OUTPUT_LOST` and `OUTPUT_BACK` in the journal bracket it. `cargo xtask measure` reads it.
@item ask-detect
question latency (measured on the reference machine). `ask_detect_ms` of the initrd splash report of a reference boot with a LUKS root: the `ask.*` file's last write to the agent opening the question, both on `CLOCK_REALTIME`. `cargo xtask measure` reads it.
@item grab-release
grab release latency (measured on the reference machine). `grab_release_ms` of the initrd splash report of a reference boot with a LUKS root: the agent frame that sends the answer and releases the keyboards at its end, an upper bound on reply to release. `cargo xtask measure` reads it.
@item overlay-entry
journal overlay latency (measured on the reference machine). `overlay_entry_ms` of the splash reports of a reference boot with the overlay shown (Escape) while the boot logs: an entry's `__MONOTONIC_TIMESTAMP` to the frame that takes it, entries under a prompt left out. `cargo xtask measure` reads it.
@end table
